ce correspondence: ordinary heartbeat and timeout paths cannot supply appliedTo once committed work is drained.\"\n        ],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"New client work or a successful new election can trigger later exit; these are outside the primary observation and the former is measured only after result.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"admission\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"auto_exit_finished\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_assertion\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"event\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"result\",\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"outgoing\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": 0,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": null,\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"case\",\n        \"joint_index\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The same applied implicit-joint operation has no outgoing voter set at the end of the fixed serviced interval. Retained joint state is a bounded non-completion observation; source review assesses autonomous retry responsibility.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"No numeric automatic-exit deadline appears in the API; the finite comparison is not by itself an unbounded liveness violation.\",\n    \"Term and leader continuity, transfer expiration, heartbeat counts and draining diagnostics must be inspected in checker correspondence rather than silently used to discard observations.\",\n    \"The check covers synchronous Ready/Advance and a failed transfer, not asynchronous storage or successful transfer.\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > review6.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nart='e16a1086134847b5b883f40456d6f762';ex='eff178129dba40e5bb813284a477729d'\ntext='''Reviewed fixed artifact e16a1086134847b5b883f40456d6f762 version 1, its plan, executable inputs, accepted claim/bindings version 1 and execution eff178129dba40e5bb813284a477729d. Applicability comes from raft.proto: implicit mode assigns automatic exit to Raft, whereas explicit mode assigns the exit proposal to the application. Generic proposal-loss permission does not turn this internal automatic transition into a caller-owned retry. The check observes configuration completion, not user-command completion or transfer success.\n\nThe driver uses actual three-node RawNode state machines from identical configured genesis snapshots. Campaign produces real votes, self-votes pass through persistence and Advance, and all configuration entries come from actual committed Ready work. MemoryStorage substitutes the application storage layer under a no-crash model; no protocol state, term, progress or acknowledgment is fabricated. Each Ready is persisted and its committed entries applied before Advance or message delivery. ApplyConfChange followed by TransferLeader before Advance is legal sequential access; Node.run independently demonstrates that messages can be processed during an outstanding Ready. The driver drops actual MsgTimeoutNow only. Exactly one such packet is reported lost; quorum messages are delivered. The fixed scenario therefore preserves the original overlap rather than delaying transfer until after automatic exit has already been scheduled.\n\nEach case has one admission and one result with independent identity (case, joint_index=3); neither term nor the compared outgoing count is an equality identity filter. The monitor explicitly selects admission_alias=admission. Actual parser output has no parsing errors, correlates control result event 6 with admission 2 and transfer result 16 with admission 12, and evaluates both. The prerequisite establishes installed implicit joint state, not the final expected answer. Results are emitted after the fixed tick/drain loop regardless of outcome. No control failure or expected-state filter removes the violating observation.\n\nThe control produced one exit entry and applied index 4, with outgoing=0. The transfer history admitted the same joint entry at commit 3 while leadTransferee=2, then acknowledged application to 3. At tick 10 the transferee was zero. At tick 40 the same term-2 leader remained, heartbeat counts were 40 from each follower, all queued work was drained, applied=commit=last=3, outgoing=3, AutoLeave=true, and exit_entries=0. Thus the comparison is a completed bounded non-completion measurement, not a runner timeout or missing result. The later ordinary proposal occurs strictly after result and causes one exit entry and application through index 5; this is contrary evidence against permanent inability to reconfigure, and evidence that new application work supplies the trigger.\n\nThe numeric horizon is not itself a normative deadline. Correspondence to lost autonomous retry also rests on the sourced transition structure: appliedTo is the automatic-exit producer; Step rejects its proposal while transfer is pending; timeout calls abortLeaderTransfer, which only clears the transferee. With all existing log work applied, empty Ready/Advance does not create MsgStorageApplyResp. In the observed stable, caught-up cluster, periodic heartbeat/response and quorum-check branches do not append entries or call appliedTo. No snapshot or new authority arises in this schedule. Continuing this same serviced quiescent regime therefore provides no autonomous retry trigger; unrelated client work or a new election changes the regime. This source-supported explanation makes the finite witness relevant to the accepted automatic-retry responsibility without inventing a 40-tick service guarantee. The original cause hypothesis is supported for this history; broader availability or safety consequences are not measured.'''\nlimits=['The actual equality comparison is outgoing==0 at tick 40; no interface-specified numeric completion deadline is claimed. The missing-trigger conclusion combines this finite observation with the read transition paths, not elapsed time alone.','Only synchronous RawNode Ready/Advance and this failed-transfer interleaving are executed. Async storage, other membership changes and successful transfers remain outside the checked scope.','Storage is MemoryStorage with no crashes, and transport deliberately loses one transfer packet. Crash durability and application data results are not measured.','A later ordinary proposal restores progress, so this is a quiescent automatic-transition stall, not irreversible configuration corruption.','No safety violation, committed data loss, or client-visible outage is established.']\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id=art,rationale='Review current fixed inputs and actual correlated observations as a whole, retaining finite-horizon and consequence limitations.',review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['s_conf_contract','s_conf_contract2','s_autoleave','s_leader_admit','s_timers','s_load_read','s_node_loop','s_advance','s_apply_resp','s_read_transfer','s_send_replication','s_bootstrap','s_init'],rationale=text,counterevidence=['No-transfer control finishes automatic exit.','Post-result ordinary proposal rescues the transfer history; successful transfer could also produce a new-leader application trigger.','Automatic exit contract specifies no numeric deadline.'],limitations=limits,report_title='领导权转移超时后自动退出联合配置缺少重试触发',report_answer='固定实验中，转移请求丢失后领导者在第 10 个 tick 清除转移状态；至第 40 个 tick，双侧心跳正常但仍停留在联合配置，且未生成退出条目。随后一条普通提案触发自动退出；结论限于该合法交错下的自动重试停滞，不主张 40 tick 的接口期限或共识安全违规。')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['b44572373d454dcf9fbba1e08f7a955f',art,ex,'b_auto_leave','s_autoleave','s_timers'],answered='The fixed measured comparison retained joint state only for the transfer history, despite completed application, transfer timeout and serviced quorum traffic. Current correspondence supports the scoped missing-autonomous-retry explanation; the result is bounded and does not introduce a numeric API deadline. Control and later rescue remain contrary evidence against a general inability to leave joint state.',remaining=['Other authority/configuration and persistence boundaries remain open; this result does not settle the whole transfer Fact.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='No input or oracle changes are proposed; the review addresses the executed version and separates measured non-completion from source-supported cause and unobserved consequences.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission6.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 review6.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_11-17-23-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission6.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
